TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Inbound handoff is at-most-once across crash/watchdog kill: the poll arm (c2c_relay_connector.ml:2777-2821) clears rows on the relay, filters in memory, then appends locally - a SIGALRM force-exit, crash, or OOM between relay-clear and append_to_local_inbox loses that batch silently. Ephemeral rows have no archive copy, so the loss is unrecoverable. The hang watchdogs whole purpose is to kill the process at an arbitrary point inside the pass, so this window is regularly exercised.

## Fix direction

peek -> persist locally -> poll (the same persist-first contract the repo mandates for the Hermes/agy delivery paths).

## Evidence

Connector review 2026-09-17.